From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Stingler <roman.stingler@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: glymur-a16: drop com_aux from usb_2_qmpphy

The usb_2_qmpphy is a DisplayPort-only instance with no DWC3 behind it. Its
com_aux (gcc_usb3_tert_phy_com_aux_clk) never leaves halt because the
tertiary block's power/reset is brought up by the DWC3 the other PHYs have,
so qmp_combo_com_init() fails with -EBUSY and the onboard HDMI PHY never
initialises.

The clk bulk get is optional, so drop com_aux from this node; the PHY then
initialises cleanly (HDMI-A-1 connected, EDID/modes read). Remove once the
qmp-combo USB-clock split (Wesley Cheng) is upstream.

Signed-off-by: Roman Stingler <roman.stingler@gmail.com>
---
 .../dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts          | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts
@@ -1552,6 +1552,11 @@
 	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l4f_e1>;
 	refgen-supply = <&vreg_l4f_e1>;
 
+	clocks = <&gcc GCC_USB3_TERT_PHY_AUX_CLK>,
+		 <&tcsr TCSR_USB4_2_CLKREF_EN>,
+		 <&gcc GCC_USB3_TERT_PHY_PIPE_CLK>;
+	clock-names = "aux", "ref", "usb3_pipe";
+
 	/delete-property/ mode-switch;
 	/delete-property/ orientation-switch;
 
-- 
